From: Gryphfield
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Preserve the native TSD in repaired full signal contexts.

EXPERIMENTAL, CI/review only. Do not ship in a release.

The selective CrossOver GS-model port restores the native TSD on signal entry.
When invalid-GS recovery recognizes a corrupt interrupted base in a full
context, update that saved base too. A host restoring the full state on
sigreturn must not reinstall the corrupt value. Contexts without GSBASE still
avoid blind retries. No Linux or FreeBSD path changes.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -2382,7 +2382,9 @@
 #elif defined(__NetBSD__)
     sysarch( X86_64_SET_GSBASE, &data->teb );
 #elif defined(__APPLE__)
-    /* init_handler() has restored GSBASE to pthread_teb. */
+    /* Preserve the repaired native base when the full context is restored. */
+    ((_STRUCT_MCONTEXT64_FULL *)ucontext->uc_mcontext)->__ss.__gsbase =
+        (ULONG_PTR)amd64_thread_data( data )->pthread_teb;
 #endif
     return TRUE;
 }
